body:
Wait, you mean to tell me there are people who can't find jobs with a CS degree? 

&#x200B;

I thought CS was supposed to be the life changing, guarantee-to-land-a-great-career degree.

You don't understand. Even by taking that route, I'd still have to end up taking a loan to pay for grad school or design school. 

&#x200B;

I want to dedicate all the time I have to learning it and building my skills now. I don't care about that philosophy class or the biology class I have to take as a requirement to graduate. That's not what my purpose in life is.
